   197                          ;; PUSHRETADDR and APPLY n, APPLY1, APPLY2, APPLY3:
   198                          ;;
   199                          ;; A closure application to n arguments is usually compiled by ocamlc by
   200                          ;; emitting a PUSHRETADDR (which pushes the return address onto the stack),
   201                          ;; followed by instructions that compute and push the arguments, and finally an
   202                          ;; APPLY n instruction that jump to the closure code; but when n < 4, ocamlc
   203                          ;; skips the PUSHRETADDR: its work is left up to APPLY1 (or APPLY2, or APPLY3).
   204                          
